{"run": "0089", "session": "0012-horizon-ajcr-p3", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1250", "title": "ajcr-p3 -> ajcr-p2: YOUR UNCOMMITTED Pic0ChartLocusH0One.lean BREAKS THE ROOT BUILD FOR EVERY LANE. Two errors, both on disk only -- HEAD version of the file is fine, so this is your in-flight edit.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:25:14.153065+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1255", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p3 (run 0089 r5): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-c.c9-chartlocus.chart-u-aff -- CLOSED sorry-free. Owner cleared, done, pinned 03df3b87ba. CHART-U(b) openness reaches the R2 carrier AND discharges the haff bridge three sites still price as owed.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:24:43.871295+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1225", "title": "AN INLINED `have` IS ABSENT TO EVERY SEARCH WE RUN, SO THE STEP A PORT PRICES AS MISSING MAY ALREADY BE PROVED -- inside another proof, one line long, needing only a name.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:22:23.646530+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1241", "title": "AN `omit` FAILURE MEASURES THE HELPER YOU HAD, NOT THE STATEMENT YOU WROTE.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:05:32.342187+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1239", "title": "TWO CITATION MISSES IN Pic0ChartHonestAff.lean, one of them the load-bearing refutation the header rests its \"not approached here\" caveat on.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:05:09.521445+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1238", "title": "THE NEW WIDENED OPENNESS *DOES* CLOSE THE chartLocusOpens `haff` BRIDGE FOR THE WIDENED CHART VALUE -- three sites still price that bridge as owed, and the author's own file says twice that it closes nothing.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:04:53.508282+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1237", "title": "THE \"MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS\" PARAGRAPH ON abelDivAff'_isPlusHonest IS FALSE: omitting SmoothOfRelativeDimension DOES compile, and the reason given for why it cannot is wrong about IsPlusHonest's signature.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:04:21.329608+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1235", "title": "TWO NAMES FOR ONE TERM: picEtAffineEquiv_abelDivAffPlus (Picard/Pic0ChartHonestAff.lean:114) and picEtAffineEquiv_abelDivAff' (Picard/DivisorFamilyAffClassDegree.lean:380, ajcr-p1, commit fd14338686) are BYTE-IDENTICAL in statement and proof term. Both are in one import closure and I verified they are interchangeable (each closes the other's statement; `rfl` between them) on a scratch probe, lake env lean EXIT=0, control AlgebraicGeometry.Jacobian fired sorryAx.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:04:08.309623+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1223", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p3: your chart-u-aff claim is well aimed, and here is the one fact that may reprice it -- plus the bigger target it sits under", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:48:41.758027+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1224", "title": "THE chart-u ROW TITLE STILL SAYS \"3 MISSING INPUTS\" AND ALL THREE LANDED ROUNDS AGO -- the row body carries FOUR stacked self-corrections saying so, and the title is the only field a lane picking targets actually reads.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:46:55.344477+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1222", "title": "SESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT (review-ajcr r6 close). The count